{"shortDescription":"Reporting season winners are still holding the top of the overbought list, led by Ramsay Health Care for a third straight week. The oversold list tells the opposite story, dominated by rate-sensitive real estate and a consumer that continues to struggle.The 14-day Relative Strength Index is a momen…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Reporting season winners are still holding the top of the overbought list, led by Ramsay Health Care for a third straight week. The oversold list tells the opposite story, dominated by rate-sensitive real estate and a consumer that continues to struggle."]},{"type":"p","children":["The 14-day Relative Strength Index is a momentum indicator that measures the magnitude and speed of recent price changes to assess whether or not a stock is overbought or oversold. An RSI of 70 or above is considered to be overbought, which means the stock is rising too quickly and likely to experience a pullback. Meanwhile, an RSI of 30 or below is considered to be oversold, which means the stock is falling too quickly and is likely to experience a rebound."]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Overbought ASX 200 Stocks"]},{"type":"p","children":["Ramsay Health Care has now topped the overbought list for three straight weeks, a reminder of what a genuine beat can do to a stock. The FY26 result and guidance (27-Aug) featured:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Group underlying EBIT up 11.5% to $1,162.2m vs $1,082m ests (7% beat)"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Underlying NPAT up 20.6% to $365.4m, or up 23% in constant currency, with every region growing earnings"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Full year dividend up 13.8% to 91 cps vs 85 cps ests (7% beat)"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["FY27 guidance points to further earnings growth and margin improvement in Australia and both UK businesses, with capex falling to $480–520m"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["For context, Ramsay has gone nowhere for more than a decade and sits about 30% below its April 2022 record high even on a total return basis. The company spent that decade buying growth offshore, and acquisitions in France and the UK never delivered it, while wage growth and the fallout from the pandemic continued to weigh on the broader sector. The Santé separation and improving Australian margins now point to a simpler business emerging."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, the ASX 200 dipped 2.9% last week so very few stocks withstood the broader tide. What remains overbought is mostly energy, spanning oil and gas, refiners and coal, plus reporting season winners like Ansell, Reliance and AMP."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-header","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["Ticker"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["Company"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["RSI"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["1 Week %"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["1 Month %"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","params":{"colspan":1},"children":["Close Price"]}]}]},{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["RHC"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Ramsay Health Care "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["79"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["2.4%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["19.3%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$53.55"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["NHC"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["New Hope "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["72"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3.8%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["17.9%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$6.33"]}]